    "inputHash": "sha256:25b8ffa8e2486354b93fe99bac33fb7ca27ca28dc470e9dc900df985cc98cf4f",
    "notes": "Farringdon’s surface interchange includes the heritage Cowcross headhouse, modern hall, two glazed canopy families, the low western ticket hall and lift shafts, Bloom and the complete Kaleidoscope host at Long Lane. The short thresholds, aprons and lobby recesses approximate current street grades using the standard host terrain and PMTiles pavement. Canopy profiles and underground rail levels are visual estimates. The western low ticket hall roof and Bloom height are inferred from current street and aerial photographs. The model shows the above-ground building envelopes and recessed doors. Platform interiors, escalators, train service and street furnishings use the host scene."
  },
